ggml-cpu repack: run MoE expert matmuls (MUL_MAT_ID) as GEMM on groups of 4 routed rows

Upstream b12032 calls one GEMV per routed token per expert, even in a 512-token prefill.
This packs each expert's rows 4 at a time (q8_0x4) and calls the repacked GEMM; the tail rows keep the GEMV.

Measured (2026-11-02/03): Ling-3.0-tiny Q4_0, perplexity identical (9.2871 on 8 chunks, desktop).
Pixel 10, 6 threads, pp512: 167 -> 201 tok/s at depth 0, 88 -> 115 tok/s at depth 1100. Decode unchanged.
Upstream PR: not opened yet.

